Description: a layer-surface inhibitor blocks every keybinding
 The Deskflow capture strip of thinfloe-menu is an overlay layer surface
 that takes the keyboard exclusively while the pointer is on an attached
 device. With 0004 an inhibitor on a layer surface was ignored, and the
 media key bindings carry allowWhenInhibited="yes" (0006), so the volume
 and brightness keys changed the local machine instead of reaching the
 device, even over an X11 keyboard grab.
 .
 An inhibitor on a layer surface is now activated and stays in the wlroots
 manager's list until it or its surface goes. While the seat's keyboard
 focus is a layer surface with such an inhibitor, no keybinding runs,
 allowWhenInhibited ones included, and every key goes to that surface.
 Inhibitors on views behave as before.
 .
 thinfloe-specific: not proposed for upstream inclusion, see Forwarded below.
Author: ThinFloe maintainers
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
